# Do Vale Studio 4 Engineering Rules

This is a professional native NLE.

Read these files before major implementation work:

- PROJECT_CONTEXT.md
- ARCHITECTURE.md
- DEVELOPMENT.md
- PERFORMANCE.md
- ROADMAP.md

The project is GPU-first.

The media pipeline must not assume CPU RGBA frames.

Do not use HTML video elements.

Do not use browser video rendering.

Do not move video rendering into egui.

egui is the application UI, not the video compositor.

Hardware decoding must be preferred when available.

Avoid GPU → CPU → GPU transfers.

Do not claim zero-copy unless the frame actually remains GPU-resident.

Do not add proxies as a primary solution for performance problems.

Do not rewrite architecture without explaining the reason.

Before major changes:

1. inspect the existing code
2. explain the proposed architecture
3. identify performance implications
4. identify threading implications
5. identify memory ownership
6. implement incrementally
7. run tests
8. update documentation

Performance-critical code must be measurable.

Avoid per-frame allocations.

Avoid blocking the UI thread.

Playback has priority over background processing.

Keep core domain logic independent from UI and FFmpeg.

Use small, testable modules.

Prefer explicit types and errors over hidden state.
